id: god-strike
name: God Strike
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
profile: any
usageLimit: 1/round
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki (maneuvers.mjs whyNotGod). "Upon gaining access to this
# God Maneuver, select a Profile" - asked at its first use and kept on the Maneuver (godStrikeProfile), changeable on
# its sheet as the Tail Attack's tail is. "Use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. Apply the
# selected Profile to that Attacking Maneuver" - the Basic Attack made with any Profile, as ever, and the selected one
# applied on top of it (the user's ruling): an applied Profile, as Multi-Profile's second is but not one - it stacks
# with Multi-Profile and a Super Profile, and from any Foundation, the attack's still the main Profile's
# (`appliedProfiles`, read with the second through chat.mjs extraProfilesOf). Paid twice, apart: the Basic Attack its
# own Profile's KP Cost as ever, and God Strike "1/4 (rounded up) of the KP Cost of that Profile" in Divine Ki Points
# (maneuvers.mjs godStrikeCost; the user's ruling).
godManeuver: true
godStrike: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: a Basic Attack out of sequence with the Profile you selected applied on top, for 1/4 (rounded up) of
  that Profile's KP Cost in Divine Ki Points.
text: >
  God Strike [1/Round]: Infuse your attacks with extra power thanks to your godly skill.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –DKP Cost: Varies
  –Effect: Upon gaining access to this God Maneuver, select a Profile. The DKP Cost of this Maneuver equals 1/4 (rounded
  up) of the KP Cost of that Profile. When using this Maneuver, use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence
  Maneuver. Apply the selected Profile to that Attacking Maneuver.
